%I A400237 #6 Oct 01 2026 23:40:20
%S A400237 47,191,239,397,691,797,1009,1087
%N A400237 Primes p such that 2^p-1 has a divisor d with 2*p+1 < d < 2^p-1 and d == 1+2*p (mod 2*p^2).
%C A400237 a(9) >= 1213.
%C A400237 1481, 1523, 1777, 6997, 9323, 9613 and 144629 are also terms.
%H A400237 Mers Project, <a href="https://mers.sourceforge.io/lowM.txt">Known information for Mersenne numbers with exponents below 200000</a>.
%H A400237 S. S. Wagstaff, Jr., <a href="https://homes.cerias.purdue.edu/~ssw/cun/pmain126.txt">Main Tables from the Cunningham Project</a>.
%e A400237 For a(1)=47, d=4513=2*47*(47+1)+1 is a prime divisor of 2^47-1.
%o A400237 (PARI) isok(p) = { if(!isprime(p), return(0)); my(M=2^p-1); fordiv(M, d, if(2*p+1<d && d<M && (d-2*p-1)%(2*p^2)==0, return(1))); return(0); }
%Y A400237 Cf. A001348, A065341, A135975, A398494, A399571.
%K A400237 nonn,more,new
%O A400237 1,1
%A A400237 _A. Lamek_, Sep 21 2026
